# securityd and secd are HELD BACK, and they are the last two Security install entries.
#
# Their archives all build now (security_tokend_client, securityd_server, securityd_ucspc,
# securitydservice_client), and securityd_exe gets past its generated <self.h> once
# securitydmig_self is in its gen_srcs. What stops it is the NEXT generated include dir:
# the reference puts a securityd_client/ directory on its include path whose every header
# is MIG output, the same shape SecurityTokend/mig had. buck-port.py reports it as
# "no framework root for securityd_client" because its resolver only knows how to add
# FRAMEWORK roots, and this is not one.
#
# secd fails differently, on undefined symbols, and has not been diagnosed.
#
# Both want the same treatment SecurityTokend just got: a mig_gen for the definition, wired
# in through extra-deps.json as a gen:// entry, with the include dir coming from the
# generated tree rather than from a source glob.



