# The COCOTRON cone is held back: Onyx2D, CoreGraphics, CoreText, QuartzCore, CoreData and
# AppKit. Cocoa is in (it is an umbrella whose single source exports nothing, which the
# reference produces too).
#
# They do not fail for want of a framework root, which is what buck-port.py knows how to
# fix. They fail on Objective-C header CASCADES: one missing framework header makes
# Foundation's own headers stop parsing, and the resulting torrent of "unknown type name
# NSMutableArray" fills clang's -ferror-limit before the single actionable
# "Security/Security.h file not found" is ever emitted. buck-port reads the first error, so
# it sees the cascade and gives up, and seeding the obvious framework deps by hand does not
# converge either.
#
# The fix belongs in buck-port.py: build the resolver's probe with -ferror-limit=0 (or
# retry once with it) so the actionable error is in the output at all. Until then this cone
# is hand work, and six frameworks in //src/darwin/frameworks wait on it (AVKit, CoreVideo,
# HIServices, ImageIO, OpenGL, Quartz).

